# NCIG v0.22.6 — real-building detection and shell geometry

## What changed

### Walkable doorway geometry

Generated corridor doors now use a 1.25 m × 2.20 m opening. The opening is cut only through the corridor-facing wall, while the 0.80 m band above the door is filled with a solid wall header and receives matching collision.

Detected exterior entrances create a separate facade opening in the room that actually owns the entrance. The exterior wall therefore stays solid everywhere else.

Door leaves are render-only unless a harvested mesh is explicitly marked as collisionless. This prevents a static door_piece from blocking a procedurally open doorway.

### Wall rendering

The shell rejects common decorative wall fragments such as protectors, addons, grates, bars, door modules and window modules when a usable full wall candidate exists.

Very thin runtime walls can receive an inverted visual face as a fallback for one-sided materials.

The generated shell no longer adds random windows. Exterior window candidates are currently preserved as detection evidence; rendering them is deferred until the wall generator can create a real wall opening around each one.

### District-aware architecture

Architecture family selection now considers structural coverage, dimensions, building type, detected district and deterministic per-building variation. The kit remains coherent while comparable buildings can use different compatible families.

## Automatic building workflow

NCIG expects the external world to be supplied as exported .streamingsector JSON. The detector does not require a hand-authored buildings.json.

Command:

.\tools\prepare_detected_buildings_remote.cmd https://github.com/Guarrazo/harvest C:\CyberpunkExports\sectors 10

The directory must contain JSON exports of the relevant base-game sectors. The workflow loads the sectors, identifies exterior architecture and entrances, rejects obvious non-building evidence, checks existing interior evidence, estimates an oriented footprint, preserves detected entries/windows, assigns type and district, and converts sufficiently supported candidates into building anchors.

Generated outputs:

- build\auto_building_candidates.json
- build\auto_buildings.json
- build\generated_auto\layouts.json
- build\real_architecture_remote\architecture_assembly_auto.json

## Limitation

A sector export is still required. The repository cannot contain Night City's game-world data. Once the relevant sectors are exported, the detection/classification/generation pipeline is automatic.